---
version: 2.0.2
title: concise classes: missing types and explicit constructors
file: ./test/concise_class_test.gleam
test_name: invalid_concise_classes_snapshot_test
---
Source:
module main

class User(name: String, age) {
  new(name, age) {
    self.name = name
  }
}

---
error: concise class fields need a type
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:3:26
  │
3 │ class User(name: String, age) {
  │                          ─┬─
  │                           ╰─ `age` has no type
  ╰─

Each field of a concise class becomes an immutable field, so it is written `name: Type`.

error: concise classes cannot declare `new`
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:4:3
  │
4 │   new(name, age) {
  │   ────────┬───────
  │           ╰─ the constructor is generated from the fields
5 │     self.name = name
6 │   }
  │   ─
  ╰─

`User` declares its fields after its name, so Pooka generates a constructor that assigns them. Custom construction needs the full class form.

help: Declare the fields with `let` in the body and write `new` yourself.

Found 2 errors.

